 from one hose to another  without any major changes now  let us move into our next section what  is  docker architecture docker is a client  server app docker daemon serves your  application to create  deploy shutdown etc and the docker  client communicates with the daemon  to manage its services client and server  are found in docker engine docker engine  or  docker is a client server application  that builds and executes containers  using docker components  now we know the major components of  docker what are the  other components which are used to build  and execute docker containers  well the other two components you need  to know are  the docker image and docker registry  the docker image is a template of  instructions that are used to create  containers  image is a read only pattern that is  used to build a container  the image can contain an apache tomcat  or kafka  with ubuntu operating system you can add  update and share your images an image is  built using a file called  dockerfile docker image has multiple  layers  whenever a developer builds a container  a new docker layer is automatically  created on top of image layers  and it is called as a container layer a  docker image provides a separate  read or write layer to each container  and whenever a user makes a change to  the container  that gets reflected upon the specific  container layer alone  now moving forward let's understand what  a docker registry is  docker registry is a service to the host  and it distributes  docker images amongst users a repository  is  a collection of docker images in  registry  a user can distinguish between docker  images with their tag names  docker has its own cloud-based registry  called docker hub  where users can store and distribute  container images  docker registry has public and private  repositories  in registry push and pull commands are  used to interact with docker images  the docker registry has two basic  commands one  is the push command and another is the  pull command  push command basically stores a docker  image and docker registry  whereas the pull command retrieves an  image from the docker registry  in simple terms a docker registry is a  storage  and content delivery service that holds  a bunch of docker images stored in  different tagged  versions a docker workflow is a sequence  of actions on registries  images and containers it allows a team  of developers to create containers based  on a customized image  pulled from a registry and deployed run  them  on a host server moving ahead we have  our next question that is  who uses docker increased running  capacity is just  one example of how docker is often  preferred choice over virtual machines  the famous global researcher gartner  predicts by the year 2023  more than 50 percent of the companies  will be adopting  docker containers in production however  a serverless container like docker will  have the revenue  from a small base of 465 million us  dollars in 2020  to reach to 944 million dollars in the  year 2024  let's move ahead and see what all  companies are using docker  some of the famous companies that use  docker for the growth  of their business are spotify yelp  adb ebay expedia  groupon bbc facebook  linkedin and also other companies like  the new york times  oxford university press paypal sage  shopify uses docker now  let's understand why expedia uses docker  and how does docker bring benefits to  their business  expedia has more than 9 000 docker  containers running in aws  ecs service expedia chose docker  to speed up the building and deploying  process of the application  which was possible due to the various  docker components like  docker registry and docker swarm now  let us look into the demo in which we  will be creating a docker file  and we will also be executing a few doc  commands  suppose you have set up your development  environment and the workload should be  like  first to create an image and then dock a  file  for each component of your application  we need to create containers and execute  the required commands and in the end  test share and deploy a complete  containerized  application in this demo let us focus on  step one  and step two first create a docker file  in case you have some source code and a  docker file then proceed to build your  first  docker image and ensure that the  containers which are launched from those  images  work correctly then let's check if we  already have any docker images as a  result  we can see no images are present here so  let's create a new one  to create a new docker image execute  this command  this downloading process may take a  while  now when you execute the command you can  see a list of docker images on the  screen  now among these two images let's delete  one named simplylearn  if you execute docker rm  simplylearn which is the remove command  as a result  one of your docker images will be  deleted  in case you want to remove ubuntu from  docker image  that can also be done by executing the  docker image  rm ubuntu command  moving on to the next one let's see a  few docker container commands  so now before executing container  commands  let's first pull jenkins from the docker  hub  now the files are being downloaded from  the hub  so let's wait for this full activity to  get completed  so once the process is done execute the  command  docker images here  you can see jenkins is getting  downloaded into your docker system  now let's create a container out of that  so execute the command docker create  jenkins this will help you create  a docker container now when you  execute docker ps space  hyphen a you can see a container which  is in the created mode  in case you want to start a container  execute the command  docker start file name  here our file name is tender napier  but if you want your container jenkins  to be in the running state type docker  run  jenkins now you can see the process has  started  so let's wait for a while  so this